        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Don Johnson, Jeanne Tripplehorn, Sharon Lawrence, John Heard, Arliss Howard\n- Products: Word of Honor (2003 film), Miami Vice, Nash Bridges\n- Roles: James \"Sonny\" Crockett\n- Topics: American television films, acting, television series, awards, motorsports\n\nFacts:\n- Don Johnson was born on December 15, 1949, and he is an American actor, producer, director, singer, and songwriter.\n- Don Johnson played James \"Sonny\" Crockett in the 1980s television series Miami Vice.\n- Don Johnson had the title lead role in the 1990s cop series Nash Bridges.\n- Don Johnson won a Golden Globe for his role in Miami Vice.\n- Don Johnson was the American Power Boat Association's 1988 World Champion of the Offshore World Cup.\n- Don Johnson received a star on the Hollywood Walk of Fame.\n- Word of Honor is an American television film that was released in 2003.\n- Word of Honor stars Don Johnson, Jeanne Tripplehorn, Sharon Lawrence, John Heard, and Arliss Howard.",
